<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<PathAssistant xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!--
        The BUY-SIDE NDA path, for the Acquisition_NDA record type.
        Four steps: Pending -> Sent -> Received -> Signed (decision D14.1).

        Pending, Sent and Signed are copied BYTE-IDENTICAL - <fieldNames> AND <info> text -
        from the now-deactivated NDA_Path. Nothing was reworded: the Tranche 2 discipline was
        that a carried-forward step must stay identical unless the step genuinely does not
        exist on that record type, and all three of these do.

        RECEIVED IS THE ONE NEW STEP, and it is the only new content in this file. It sits
        between Sent and Signed and names the distinction the source document draws at Part 1
        lines 38 and 41 - "NDA not yet received from broker" vs "the NDA has been received".
        Its <fieldNames> are Date_Sent__c and OneDrive_URL__c because those are the two fields
        a user actually works at this point: confirm how long it has been out, and attach the
        returned document. Counter_Signed_Date__c is NOT surfaced here - it is disposition-only
        (on an acquisition DPEG is the party signing, not the counter-signer).

        DELIBERATELY NOT REWORDED, though it now reads slightly early: the Sent step still says
        "follow up until it comes back signed", where the process now has it come back RECEIVED
        first and Signed after. Editing it would be an unrequested change to carried-forward
        text, which is the exact discipline Tranche 2's review credited. If the business wants
        it reworded, that is a separate one-line change.

        Not Sent and Declined do not appear because the Acquisition_NDA record type restricts
        them out; they belong to NDA_Path_Disposition.

        Step ORDER in this file is the intended path order. Runtime display order comes from the
        Status__c picklist value order (sorted=false), which is Pending, Sent, Received, Signed,
        Not Sent, Declined - so the four values this type exposes already fall in the right
        sequence with no reordering of the master value set.

        =====================================================================
        AMENDED 2026-08-16 - SEQUENCE REVERSED. THE PARAGRAPHS ABOVE DESCRIBE THE SUPERSEDED
        D14.1 ORDER AND ARE RETAINED VERBATIM AS THE RECORD OF WHAT CHANGED.
        =====================================================================

        THE SEQUENCE IS NOW Pending -> Received -> Signed -> Sent. 'Sent' IS NOW TERMINAL, not
        'Signed'. The process direction itself reversed: the broker's NDA now ARRIVES first
        (Pending), DPEG receives it (Received) and signs it (Signed), then DPEG sends the signed
        copy back to the broker (Sent) - the opposite of the D14.1 process above, where DPEG
        sent the NDA out first and it came back signed.

        REVIEWED REWORD DONE 2026-08-16 - the paragraph this replaces flagged all four <info>
        texts as carried over unchanged and describing the superseded direction. That pass is now
        complete: Pending, Received and Sent were reworded to match the new direction (the
        broker's NDA arriving, being reviewed for DPEG signature, and the signed copy going back
        out, respectively); Signed's text was left unchanged, as flagged, because it is
        direction-neutral and needed no rework.

        Date_Sent__c WAS ALSO REMOVED FROM THE Received STEP'S <fieldNames> in the same pass
        (2026-08-16). Under the new order nothing has been sent to anyone by the time a record
        reaches Received - it is the SECOND step, right after Pending - so stamping a "sent" date
        there no longer makes sense; OneDrive_URL__c (the returned document) stays.

        ⚠ AMENDED 2026-08-16 (SAME-DAY FOLLOW-UP) - THE GAP THE PARAGRAPH ABOVE FLAGGED IS NOW
        CLOSED. The Received step was left with no date field to record its own result when the
        sequence reversal shipped, tracked as FSD §27.6. NDA__c.Date_Received__c now exists
        (objects/NDA__c/fields/Date_Received__c.field-meta.xml - a plain Date, manually stamped,
        matching the shape of Date_Sent__c and Date_Signed__c on this object) and is added to this
        step's <fieldNames> below, ahead of OneDrive_URL__c. Not surfaced on
        NDA_Path_Disposition - see that file's own comment for why the disposition side does not
        carry it.

        ⚠ THE MASTER-FIELD-ORDER NOTE ABOVE IS ALSO NOW STALE. That paragraph states this file's
        step order happened to already match the Status__c FIELD's master value order (Pending,
        Sent, Received, Signed, ...), so no separate reorder of the master field was ever
        needed. That coincidence is GONE: this change reordered only this file's
        <pathAssistantSteps> and the Acquisition_NDA record type's own picklistValues order, not
        the master Status__c field (objects/NDA__c/fields/Status__c.field-meta.xml), so the
        master order and this file's new step order no longer match.

        🔴 THE PATH BUBBLES ARE VERIFIED CORRECT (2026-08-16 follow-up). <pathAssistantSteps>
        order in this file is Pending -> Received -> Signed -> Sent, which IS the intended
        sequence per the reversal above - confirmed, not amended, since it already read that way.

        🔴 THE DROPDOWN IS A DIFFERENT QUESTION AND HAS A GENUINE, UNRESOLVABLE-BY-ORDERING
        CONSTRAINT (2026-08-16 follow-up, replacing the "needs a decision from whoever requested
        it" note this paragraph used to end on). The master Status__c field is deliberately NOT
        reordered to fix the acquisition dropdown, and it cannot be: the two record types need
        OPPOSITE orders on the values they SHARE. Acquisition ends ... Signed -> Sent; disposition
        ends ... Sent -> Signed (Not Sent -> Sent -> Signed, plus the Declined off-ramp - see
        NDA_Path_Disposition). One master picklist order cannot satisfy both directions for the
        same pair of values at once, so reordering the master field to put 'Sent' after 'Signed'
        for the acquisition side would necessarily put disposition's 'Sent' after its own
        'Signed' too - breaking the sell-side dropdown to fix the buy-side one. This is not a
        gap to close; it is a structural property of one shared field serving two opposite
        processes, and NDA_Path_Disposition's own comment carries the matching, now-corrected
        statement of the same constraint from the disposition side.

        WHAT IS STILL GENUINELY UNVERIFIED: whether the record type's own picklistValues order
        (in objects/NDA__c/recordTypes/Acquisition_NDA.recordType-meta.xml, already reordered to
        Pending, Received, Signed, Sent) influences the runtime Status__c DROPDOWN at all,
        independently of the master field's own value order. That needs an in-org check - open an
        Acquisition NDA record and read the Status__c dropdown's rendered order - which was not
        performed as part of this follow-up. IF the record type's order does NOT drive the
        dropdown, the acquisition dropdown order cannot be corrected without harming disposition
        (per the constraint above), and the Path bubbles - already verified correct - remain the
        authoritative visual sequence for users regardless of what the dropdown shows.
    -->
    <active>true</active>
    <entityName>NDA__c</entityName>
    <fieldName>Status__c</fieldName>
    <masterLabel>NDA Path Acquisition</masterLabel>
    <pathAssistantSteps>
        <fieldNames>Counterparty_Name__c</fieldNames>
        <fieldNames>Method__c</fieldNames>
        <info>The broker&apos;s NDA is expected but has not arrived. Confirm the counterparty and the delivery method, then chase it until it lands.</info>
        <picklistValueName>Pending</picklistValueName>
    </pathAssistantSteps>
    <pathAssistantSteps>
        <fieldNames>Date_Received__c</fieldNames>
        <fieldNames>OneDrive_URL__c</fieldNames>
        <info>The broker&apos;s NDA has arrived. Review the terms and route it for DPEG signature - NDA Signed stays FALSE at this step, so the deal cannot advance to Underwriting yet.</info>
        <picklistValueName>Received</picklistValueName>
    </pathAssistantSteps>
    <pathAssistantSteps>
        <fieldNames>Date_Signed__c</fieldNames>
        <fieldNames>NDA_Signed__c</fieldNames>
        <info>NDA fully executed. NDA Signed = TRUE is what unlocks advancing the deal to Underwriting.</info>
        <picklistValueName>Signed</picklistValueName>
    </pathAssistantSteps>
    <pathAssistantSteps>
        <fieldNames>Date_Sent__c</fieldNames>
        <fieldNames>OneDrive_URL__c</fieldNames>
        <info>Signed copy returned to the broker. This is the final step - the deal gate is already open and nothing comes back.</info>
        <picklistValueName>Sent</picklistValueName>
    </pathAssistantSteps>
    <recordTypeName>Acquisition_NDA</recordTypeName>
</PathAssistant>
